WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.824
Each run becomes an evidence package: the
kit's run as written, the drift report,

2
00:00:04.824 --> 00:00:09.151
the latest provenance from the other
kits, a manifest, and a list of file

3
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:13.850
hashes the security officer can check
with a standard tool and nothing else.

4
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:18.956
Each manifest records the hash of the
previous one, so the packages form a chain:

5
00:00:18.956 --> 00:00:22.412
a replaced package or a missing
day shows up as a break.

6
00:00:22.412 --> 00:00:24.338
The packager doesn't sign, though.

7
00:00:24.338 --> 00:00:27.101
Locked retention stops
changes after the fact,

8
00:00:27.101 --> 00:00:31.920
and signing with a key the pipeline holds
is a choice left to the security officer.
